// The cold store: 56 × 36 m of white cladding on a concrete plinth, its whole floor raised 1.2 m to the height of a
// lorry's bed. Inside, insulated walls 6.2 m high: four chambers along the north side; the aisle (z 12–16) the length
// of the building; to its south two more chambers, a cross aisle through to the dock hall, and two blast freezers;
// and the dock hall along the front (z 26–36) behind four dock doors. Each chamber has a heavy insulated door (sliding
// or swinging, shut, open or ajar by chance each round); the chambers in each pair are joined by a small door, and the
// fifth and sixth also open onto the dock hall. No windows but a few high in the dock hall: it's dark in there.
// Outside: a ramp up to the first dock door, steps up to the side doors, and a forklift ramp at the aisle's east end.
// Outer wall segments: 0 north (x 0→56), 1 east (z 0→36), 2 south (x 56→0, at_m = 56 − x), 3 west (z 36→0, at_m = 36 − z).
